From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:12:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show the selected system's extras when the tab changes

- A tab shown before gives back its extras hidden. When the cursor's index
  on the new tab matched the old one, the cursor change did not activate
  them: the selected system's panel stayed hidden (its video did not
  play) until the cursor moved. Going to a system now shows its extras.
---
 es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp b/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
index 57092bd0..2f5657e7 100644
--- a/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
@@ -450,6 +450,10 @@ void SystemView::goToSystem(SystemData* system, bool animate)
 	if (mLastCursor == -1)
 		onCursorChanged(CURSOR_STOPPED);
 
+	// The selected system's extras show: those of a tab shown before come back hidden, and a cursor already in
+	// place (the same index on both tabs) does not activate them
+	activateExtras(mCarousel.getCursorIndex());
+
 	if (!animate)
 	{
 		finishAnimation(0);
